rint\":\"e05ba8375b1c9940a3815fd5f07468886472be6a3de29b96928fe4c4155dc0e4\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Chigozie Obioma born city grew up biography\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... His two novels, The Fishermen (2015) and An Orchestra of Minorities (2019) were shortlisted for The Booker Prize and have been translated into 30 languages. He has an LA Times book prize, the prestigious Internationalerpris, FT/Oppenheimer prize for fiction, an NAACP Image award and has been nominated ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.oxbelly.com/fiction-writers-program/advisors\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d64\"},\"ref\":\"d64\",\"snippet\":\" ... Pictures at an Exhibition, orchestrated by Maurice Ravel He published Ravel's score himself and in 1930 made the first recording of it with the Boston Symphony Orchestra. The exclusive nature of his commission prompted the release of a number of contemporary versions by other arrangers until Ravel ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pictures_at_an_Exhibition\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d65\"},\"ref\":\"d65\",\"snippet\":\" ... of Maryland] is an Associate Professor who teaches Francophone literatures and cultures in French, Classics, and Romance Languages. She has published Réflexions littéraires sur l'espace public marocain dans l'uvre d'Abdellatif Laâbi (2008) on the literary work of Moroccan writer Abdellatif Laabi, founder of the New ... \",\"title\":\"https://jsp.msu.edu/faculty/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d66\"},\"ref\":\"d66\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1 in C Major, BWV 1066\\n\\nSuite for Orchestra in B Minor, BWV 1067\\n\\nSuite pour orchestre n°3 en Ré Majeur, bwv 1068\\n\\n11.11. Opera Formatting. The track title for a selection from an opera must be consistent and start with the name of the opera ... \",\"title\":\"https://help.apple.com/itc/musicstyleguide/en.lproj/static.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d67\"},\"ref\":\"d67\",\"snippet\":\" ... in Foreign Language Education from Florida International University. She has experience as a translator and a private tutor of English and Japanese for more than 20 years. She is passionate about reducing foreign language anxiety in classrooms.\\n\\nChristina Torres, Assistant Professor\\n\\nChristina Torres '13MA '22PhD was born in ... \",\"title\":\"https://cah.ucf.edu/news/welcoming-new-faculty-members-2023/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d68\"},\"ref\":\"d68\",\"snippet\":\" ... From 1904 to 1914, Brahms's friend, the music critic Max Kalbeck, published an eight volume biography of Brahms, but this has never been translated into English. Between 1906 and 1922, the Deutsche Brahms-Gesellschaft (German Brahms Society) published 16 numbered volumes of Brahms's correspondence, at least ... \",\"title\":\"https://louis.pressbooks.pub/exploringarts/chapter/575/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d69\"},\"ref\":\"d69\",\"snippet\":\" ... She currently studies with Sunghae Anna Lim and is an enthusiastic\\n\\nmember of the music community. Rachel is a volunteer violin teacher for Trenton Arts\\n\\nat Princeton, concertmaster of the Princeton University Orchestra, a member of Opus\\n\\nChamber Music Princeton, and previously a member of Princeton Camerata. In ... \",\"title\":\"https://music.princeton.edu/event/certificate-recital-ewan-curtis/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d70\"},\"ref\":\"d70\",\"snippet\":\" ... Nelson's Stardust album was inducted into the Grammy Hall of Fame in 2015.\\n\\nIn popular culture\\n\\nIn 1938, Orson Welles's radio broadcast The War of the Worlds featured an excerpt of \\\"Stardust\\\" played by the fictional Ramón Raquello Orchestra. The 1961 episode \\\"The Hit Songwriters\\\" of ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stardust_(1927_song)\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"f064516404b1c3f83622bf9cb2afac3a8f2efb0106b19bcdb5b579039675ae62\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"c2ffc9a937e05c915f4e12895c88ea7b24e3c3ff9868b905aa9166ced2128a2c\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"An Orchestra of Minorities published 2019 translated languages\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_b0df7131c6144b5bb44ee6fb"},{"content":"I have a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma was born in Akure, Nigeria. His novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. The Man Booker International Prize was created in 2005 (in the 2000s).\n\nLet me verify the key connection: In 2019 (when \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" was published), the Man Booker International Prize was won by a book released the preceding year (2018). That winner was \"Celestial Bodies\" by Jokha Alharthi, translated by Marilyn Booth. Let me verify this and check the city connection.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker International Prize 2019 winner Celestial Bodies Jokha Alharthi\", \"Jokha Alharthi born city Oman biography\", \"Celestial Bodies published 2018 2019 Jokha Alharthi\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_3f4cb11efac84b85884e4365","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma grew up city Akure biography childhood\", \"Chigozie Obioma early life Nigeria hometown\"], \"top_k\": 8}","name":"search"},"id":"call_fe039acb848a455cb5801dbd","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d71\"},\"ref\":\"d71\",\"snippet\":\" ... Celestial Bodies: A Novel, Jokha Alharthi (Oct. 15)\\n\\nThree Omani sisters grapple with love and loss as their country quickly transforms due to the rise of the oil industry. Celestial Bodies, the first novel originally published in Arabic to win the Man Booker International Prize, showcases Oman's ... \",\"title\":\"https://time.com/5661400/best-books-fall-2019/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d72\"},\"ref\":\"d72\",\"snippet\":\" ... Marilyn Booth (Catapult, Simon & Schuster)\\n\\nFrom the publisher: \\\"From Man Booker International Prize–winning author Jokha Alharthi, Bitter Orange Tree is a profound exploration of social status, wealth, desire, and female agency. It presents a mosaic portrait of one young woman's attempt to understand the roots she ... \",\"title\":\"https://arablit.org/2021/11/30/forthcoming-2022-arabic-literature-in-english-translation/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":f